---
/**
 * ACADEMICS → 01 · ACADEMIC PHILOSOPHY
 *
 * BUILT IN STAGES. The page carries, in order:
 *
 *   Banner                                 ✓ this file
 *   Teaching Philosophy                    ✓ components/academics/TeachingPhilosophy.astro
 *   Student-Centred Learning               ⏳ to design
 *   Experiential & Inquiry-Based Learning  ⏳ to design
 *   Critical Thinking & Creativity         ⏳ to design
 *   Curriculum                             ⏳ to design
 *   Affiliation Details                    ✓ components/academics/AffiliationDetails.astro
 *
 * The four outstanding sections are previewed by the four feature cards in the
 * Teaching Philosophy band, which is deliberate: the band is the page's contents
 * list as well as its opening statement. They belong BETWEEN the band and the
 * affiliation bar — the bar is the page's closing plate and should stay last.
 *
 * BANNER — PageHero, the same component every other inner page uses (History,
 * Vision and Mission, both leadership messages). This page previously opened on
 * a typographic hero of its own with no photograph, which made it the one page
 * in the section whose header did not match the rest of the site. The client
 * asked for the shared banner, so the bespoke one is gone.
 *
 * TWO DELIBERATE ABSENCES:
 *
 * · <PhilosophyConstellation /> is commented out below, not deleted — the client
 *   is taking that design to another page. Leave the import where it is.
 *
 * · NO <ChapterNav />. Every other page in this section ends on the chapter
 *   pager; the client asked for it off this one. ⚠ It was also the only link out
 *   of here to Academic Structure and the Academics overview, so this page is now
 *   a leaf: a reader arriving from search leaves via the masthead or the footer.
 *   Worth a look once the four outstanding sections land.
 *
 * ⚠ THE MEGA-MENU POINTS AT /academics/philosophy/#curriculum (see
 * data/navigation.ts). That anchor lived on the constellation, so it currently
 * resolves to the top of the page. It comes back when the Curriculum section is
 * built — give that section id="curriculum".
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import PhilosophyStory from '../../components/academics/PhilosophyStory.astro';
import banner from '../../assets/library/DSC_1225 copy.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={banner}
  />

  {/* padding-bottom: 0 — the last section in here closes on its own sand ground
      and the panel's 120px of ivory would have shown as a strip beneath it. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel phil-panel">
    {/* ⚠ ONE COMPONENT REPLACES THREE. TeachingPhilosophy, the commented-out
        PhilosophyConstellation and AffiliationDetails each carried a slice of
        the seven themes and each was built as its own band of cards. The seven
        are now one composed sequence in PhilosophyStory, which is what lets the
        openers, the triad, the collage, the timeline and the record plate share
        a single decorative language instead of three. The old components are
        left in the repo rather than deleted — nothing else imports them, so
        restoring one is a single line. */}
    <PhilosophyStory />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* div.phil-panel, not .phil-panel: it has to out-specify .u-page-panel in
     base.css, which a bare scoped class only matches rather than beats. */
  div.phil-panel { padding-bottom: 0; }
</style>
